        judges(11, 1, "Judges", 6, 12, "Jephthah's call as a mighty warrior recalls the angel's address to Gideon, another unlikely deliverer raised up by God."),
        judges(11, 8, "Judges", 10, 18, "The Gileadites' request that Jephthah lead them fulfills their earlier search for someone to command the fight against Ammon."),
        judges(11, 11, "Judges", 10, 17, "Jephthah is installed as Gilead's leader at Mizpah after Israel gathers there to face the Ammonite threat."),
        judges(11, 15, "Deuteronomy", 2, 19, "Jephthah's defense respects the boundary God gave Ammon, as Moses had commanded Israel not to seize Ammonite land."),
        judges(11, 24, "Numbers", 21, 29, "Jephthah's argument names Chemosh, the god lamented in the earlier oracle over Moab's defeat."),
        judges(11, 25, "Micah", 6, 5, "Both passages recall Balak's failed opposition to Israel, using the Moabite episode to defend God's gift of the land."),
        judges(11, 34, "Exodus", 15, 20, "Jephthah's daughter greets a victorious leader with timbrels and dancing, echoing Miriam's celebration after the Exodus."),
