        judges(18, 14, "Judges", 17, 5, "The spies' inventory of Micah's shrine identifies the cult objects introduced when Micah established his household sanctuary."),
        judges(18, 29, "Joshua", 19, 47, "Dan's renaming of Laish parallels Joshua's record that the Danites captured Leshem and named it Dan after their ancestor."),
        judges(18, 31, "Joshua", 18, 1, "Micah's image remains at Dan during the period when the legitimate tent of meeting stood at Shiloh, highlighting the competing sanctuary."),
        judges(19, 15, "Hosea", 9, 9, "Hosea cites Gibeah's corruption as the lasting example of the deep depravity displayed in this narrative."),
        judges(20, 28, "Joshua", 24, 33, "Phinehas, who ministers before the ark in this crisis, is the priest whose family inheritance and burial Joshua records."),
        judges(21, 1, "Judges", 20, 1, "The oath at Mizpah follows the national assembly that had gathered there to respond to the outrage at Gibeah."),
        judges(21, 10, "Deuteronomy", 13, 15, "The assembly's destruction of Jabesh-gilead applies the severe covenant judgment prescribed for a community judged to have committed grave unfaithfulness."),
        judges(21, 13, "Judges", 20, 47, "Israel's offer of peace addresses the six hundred Benjaminites who escaped to the rock of Rimmon after the civil war."),
        judges(21, 25, "Deuteronomy", 12, 8, "The book's closing diagnosis repeats Moses' warning against each person doing what seems right in worship."),
        judges(21, 25, "Judges", 17, 6, "The final refrain repeats the diagnosis that introduced Micah's private shrine and frames the closing stories as its consequence.")
    ]

    private nonisolated static let entriesPart21: [Entry] = [
